 from the two prior reviewer runs (which had inspected positively but lost their verdicts by backgrounding the full suite in a headless session).\n\nWhat I verified first-hand against the epic work in the primary checkout (read-only):\n\n- **Precedence** — `resolveBuildHTTPS` resolves each effective repository as: covering run-wide override → longest segment-aware `build_https` scope (reuses the generic `longestScope` shared with SSH, Spec §6.3) → anonymous. The test proves the longer of two nested scopes wins on both secret and username.\n- **Host pin (core 12.2)** — exact-equality pin at `buildhttps.go:141`; the test proves a non-covered host falls back to its own scope and a non-covered unmatched host stays anonymous.\n- **Secret hygiene** — all three carrying types keep secrets in unexported fields with String/GoString redaction; tests assert `%v`/`%+v`/`%#v` are secret-free *and* contain `<redacted>`, plus capture immutability after environment mutation. The downstream `buildrepo.HTTPSCredentials` redacts identically.\n- **Anonymous asymmetry** — unmatched selection is anonymous with the required comment explaining the deliberate difference from SSH; only a *selected* source with missing material fails closed, and all **three remedies** (set the env var / `git credential approve` / `curator config build-https login`) have gate-refuses negative tests.\n- **Transport skip** — SSH/local rows produce zero credentials, provenance, and credential-store reads even with an applicable override present.\n- **Production reachability** — capture at `cmd/curator/main.go:1354`, resolution inside `planExternalBuilds`, per-fetch binding via `externalGitTool`; the plan-carriage test drives the real entry point, so this is no orphan helper.\n\nGates: I reran the 8 focused BuildHTTPS tests myself (all pass, exit 0) and checked gofmt (clean). The full `go test ./...` (42 packages ok, exit 0) I accepted from the orchestrator's attached log after confirming **no Go source file is newer than that log** — it covers exactly the tree reviewed. Build/vet/lint exit 0 accepted from implementer evidence.\n\nBoard state: verdict artifact `TASK-260825-1lausy_review-verdict.md` attached, checklist completed, acceptance note appended, status `done` (the board took it without `commit_ack` — that gate sits on the landing task, and I supplied none per the reviewer constraint). Side effect: the story auto-promoted to `done`. One non-blocking observation is recorded in the verdict: `%x` would bypass Stringer redaction, but that holds equally for the already-landed SSH types — a codebase-wide convention question, not this task's defect.","ttft_ms":9368,"ttft_stream_ms":1593,"time_to_request_ms":37,"type":"result","duration_ms":345223,"uuid":"4ebbf6a3-aee1-4bb9-b6d2-196df1c9e7cc"}
